```text
node test/page-lifecycle.test.js
exit 1: Cannot find module '../src/pages/index/health-adapter.js'
```

The focused test file was written before the adapter/controller implementation. After the minimal implementation and `index.ux` wiring:

```text
node test/page-lifecycle.test.js
exit 0: 7 page lifecycle tests passed
```

The covered mutations are stale per-type health failure evicting a new subscription, queued old motion success/failure crossing generations, hidden recent completion updating UI, synchronous subscribe throw escaping, one unsubscribe throw aborting later types, repeated start/stop duplicating system calls, and boxing resources rearming at completion.

Release orchestration RED:

```text
node test/release-runner.test.js
exit 1: AssertionError, true !== false
```

The `true` value was `existsSync(realExpectedDestination)` after an injected staged failure. After removing the exact real destination before staging and adding temporary publication:

```text
node test/release-runner.test.js
exit 0: 6 release runner tests passed
```

Additional focused evidence:

